That breaks those two tests. Hmm.

This is an important design detail: `Recoil::default()` provides per-gear vectors of length 1 with default values; a test/struct-literal that only sets the global fields gets per-gear = [0.0] which shadows the global.

Since old *configs* deserialize with empty vectors (serde default = empty Vec), the fallback works for real old files. But in-memory literals built from `Recoil::default()` + global overrides are shadowed.

